------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled segmentation pipeline and model weights
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

medmcp-neuro-ms wraps LST-AI and redistributes the model weights its pipeline
runs on (baked into the published container image). Each component remains
under its own license and carries its own citation requirements; if you use the
results in research, please cite the underlying methods (see the "Citation"
section of README.md).

  - LST-AI (segment_ms_lesions) — MS white-matter lesion segmentation on a
    T1w + FLAIR pair; UNet3D ensemble, native PyTorch.
    MIT. https://github.com/CompImg/LST-AI
    Weights: the three-model .pt ensemble and the MNI atlas bundle, fetched
    from the CompImg/LST-AI `v2.0.0-data` release and baked into the image.
    Cite: Wiltgen, McGinnis, Schlaeger et al., "LST-AI: A deep learning
    ensemble for accurate MS lesion segmentation", NeuroImage: Clinical 42,
    103611 (2024). doi:10.1016/j.nicl.2024.103611

  - HD-BET, as the brainles_hd_bet package (skull stripping inside the LST-AI
    pipeline).
    AGPL-3.0. https://github.com/BrainLesion/HD-BET
    Weights: all five parameter folds, baked into the image. HD-BET runs
    unmodified as a component of the containerised pipeline; its complete
    source is available upstream.
    Cite: Isensee et al., "Automated brain extraction of multisequence MRI
    using artificial neural networks", Human Brain Mapping 40(17):4952-4964
    (2019). doi:10.1002/hbm.24750

  - greedy, as the picsl-greedy package (registration to MNI space).
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/pyushkevich/greedy
    Cite: Yushkevich et al., "IC-P-174: Fast Automatic Segmentation of
    Hippocampal Subfields and Medial Temporal Lobe Subregions in 3 Tesla and
    7 Tesla T2-Weighted MRI", Alzheimer's & Dementia 12:P126-P127 (2016).
    doi:10.1016/j.jalz.2016.06.205

  - FastSurfer v2.5.4 (region annotation: the seg-only FastSurferVINN
    whole-brain segmentation; no FreeSurfer license involved).
    Apache-2.0. https://github.com/Deep-MI/FastSurfer
    Weights: the FastSurferVINN (asegdkt) checkpoints, baked into the image.
    Cite both papers, as FastSurfer itself asks: Henschel et al., "FastSurfer
    — A fast and accurate deep learning based neuroimaging pipeline",
    NeuroImage 219:117012 (2020), doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2020.117012; and
    Henschel et al., "FastSurferVINN: Building resolution-independence into
    deep learning segmentation methods", NeuroImage 251:118933 (2022).
    doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2022.118933

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled libraries
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Python libraries redistributed inside the container image — including
PyTorch, nibabel, SimpleITK, torchio, and their transitive dependency
closure — each remain under their own license; the full license texts travel
with each package's distribution.
